{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When you send forth your Spirit
They are creat[Gm7]ed anew
You made it new
You re[Eb]new the face of the earth
With grace that we [Bb]receive
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
May the glory of the Lord
Endure forever[Gm7]more
May he [Eb]rejoice in his works
Who trembles the [Bb]earth and more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will sing to the Lord all my life
I [Gm7]will sing praise to my God as long as I live
[Eb]May my meditation please him
I will rejoice in the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He looks at the earth and it trembles
Touches the [Gm7]mountains and they smoke
The wicked [Eb]shall vanish from the earth
Sinners shall [Bb]be no more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will sing to the Lord all my life
I will [Gm7]sing praise to my God as long as I live
